{{- define "privacy" -}}<article><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p><strong>{{ versionLine }}</strong> This policy describes what happens to data about you when you read {{ siteName }} at <code>https://{{ siteHost .SiteURL }}</code>. It is written against the deployment rather than against a template, so every statement in it is a description of a specific configuration that you can check from the page you are reading.</p><h2>1. Summary</h2><ul><li>This site serves static files. It sets no cookies of its own, and none are set on its behalf.</li><li>There are no accounts, no logins, no forms and no user submissions, so there is no profile of you to build.</li><li>There is no analytics, no advertising, no tracking pixel, no fingerprinting and no third-party embed.</li><li>Nothing is stored on your device: no cookie, no local storage, no session storage, no cache beyond the ordinary HTTP cache your browser keeps for any file it downloads.</li><li>One thing is processed: an ordinary web-server access log that records the request, including your IP address. Section 6 describes it in full, including how long it lives and how to ask for it to be removed.</li><li>The statistics are aggregate counts. They contain no per-player record, summoner name, PUUID, account or match history, and nothing on this site can be used to look a player up.</li></ul><h2>2. Who is responsible for your data</h2><p>The controller - the person who decides what is done with the little data described here - is the operator of this site: {{ operator }}</p><p>{{ contactRoute }}</p><p>There is no data protection officer, because the processing is not of the kind that requires one: this is a non-commercial hobby site with no systematic monitoring of anyone.</p><h2>3. What this site does not collect</h2><p>The following are absent from the deployed site rather than merely unmentioned: no account system, no login, no email address collected, no contact form, no comment form, no newsletter, no search box that records what you typed, no advertising identifier, no device fingerprint, no cross-site tracking, no session identifier, no behavioural profiling and no automated decision-making about you. Nothing is asked of you in order to read a page.</p><p>If a future version adds anything that stores data on your device or sends data about you anywhere, this policy has to be updated before that version ships, and the effective date at the top of this page is how you can tell whether it has been.</p><h2>4. Cookies and local storage</h2><p>This site sets no cookies and writes nothing to your browser's local storage or session storage. There is therefore no cookie banner to dismiss, no consent prompt and nothing to opt out of. The site is a set of files: it has no server-side session, no login state and no server-side database of visitors, so it has nowhere to keep a preference about you even if it wanted one.</p><h2>5. What your browser talks to</h2><ul><li><strong>This origin, for pages.</strong> You request an HTML page and its assets (stylesheets, fonts, images from the site itself, and one small amount of JavaScript that is optional for reading the pages) from <code>lol.erik-schuetze.dev</code>. That is the request described in section 6.</li><li><strong>Riot's Data Dragon CDN, for icons.</strong> Champion, item, rune and spell icons are loaded by your browser from <code>ddragon.leagueoflegends.com</code> rather than served from this site. That request carries your IP address and your browser's user agent to Riot, under Riot's own privacy policy, and Riot Games is established in the United States, so loading an icon is a transfer of that request data outside the European Economic Area. This site is not told the result and receives nothing about it. No image is copied, re-encoded or re-served here.</li><li><strong>Nothing else.</strong> No font host, no CDN script, no embedded video or audio, no social widget, no third-party map, no CAPTCHA and no error-reporting service is requested by any page. The three font families this site uses are served from this origin under <code>/fonts/</code>.</li></ul><p>Being precise about a near miss: the operator does run a self-hosted analytics instance (Umami) elsewhere on the same home cluster, at a different hostname. This site loads no script from it and sends it nothing; if that ever changed, this policy and the site's JavaScript would change first, and the change would be visible both here and in the page source.</p><h2>6. Server logs: the one thing that is processed</h2><p>A web server records the requests it serves. The site is served by a Caddy web server running in the operator's own Kubernetes cluster, configured to write its access log to the container's standard output and to keep nothing otherwise. For each request it records what any web server records: the IP address the request came from, the time, the method and path requested, the response status and size, and the user agent your browser sent.</p><ul><li><strong>Why.</strong> To serve the pages at all, to diagnose faults (a broken page, a configuration error) and to recognise and block abuse such as a request flood. This is processing on the basis of the operator's legitimate interests in running and protecting the site (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR), and it goes no further than that.</li><li><strong>What it is not used for.</strong> Not profiling, not advertising, not analytics, not improving statistics about champions, and not combined with anything else. Nothing in the log is sold, rented, brokered or shared with any third party, and no Riot API data and no log line is ever joined to a player's record.</li><li><strong>How long.</strong> No log shipper, no log store and no retention configuration exists in the cluster, so the lines exist only in the node's container log file, which the container runtime rotates and truncates; they are lost when the container is replaced, which happens on every deployment, and on node maintenance. The practical retention is therefore days rather than months, and the operator does not go looking through them except when diagnosing a fault or an attack.</li><li><strong>Who else sees them.</strong> Only the operator, on the operator's own hardware. There is no CDN, no reverse-proxy provider, no hosting company and no log-processing service in front of this site: the address resolves to the operator's own connection, where a single proxy terminates TLS and forwards to the site. Neither the proxy nor the site sets a cookie, and the proxy is not configured to write an access log of its own.</li><li><strong>Erasing it.</strong> The logs contain no identifier that points at anything but a request, so there is nothing to look up by name. If you want a log line about your visit deleted, write to the address in section 11 with the approximate time and, if you know it, the IP address you used, and it will be removed; if the relevant lines have already rotated away, you will be told that instead of being told nothing.</li></ul><h2>7. Personal data in the statistics</h2><p>{{ noBroker }}</p><p>This is a deliberate design choice as well as a legal one. Riot's policies for third-party products prohibit exposing personal data that way, and a statistics site does not need it: {{ if .Live }}match records are reduced to counts before anything is published{{ else }}match records are reduced to counts before anything is published, and this build has no match records to reduce{{ end }}, and the identifiers that could point at a person never reach the artifacts the site serves.{{ if .Live }}The raw archive that the aggregation reads is kept for the operator's own quality control and is not served, not resold and not exposed to anyone.{{ else }}No raw match archive exists for this build, and nothing in this policy depends on one existing: the raw archive behind a live snapshot is kept for the operator's own quality control and is not served, not resold and not exposed to anyone.{{ end }}</p><h2>8. If something goes wrong</h2><p>If a breach ever affected personal data, the operator would report it to the competent supervisory authority under Article 33 GDPR within 72 hours of becoming aware of it, and would tell affected people under Article 34 where the risk to them is high. Given what is described above - a rotating server log on self-hosted hardware with no accounts, no stored user records and no third parties - there is very little that a breach could reach, which is the point of the design.</p><h2>9. Children</h2><p>This site is a statistics reference and is not directed at children, and it collects nothing from anyone of any age. Playing League of Legends requires accepting Riot Games' own terms, including its age requirements, which is between you and Riot.</p><h2>10. Your rights</h2><p>Where the GDPR applies to you, you have the right to be informed about the processing described here, to request access to personal data about you, to have it corrected or erased, to have its processing restricted, to object to processing based on legitimate interests, and to receive data you provided in a portable form. You also have the right not to be subject to a decision based solely on automated processing, and this site makes none.</p><p>In practice, there is no record of you to access, correct or export: the site stores no profile, and the only place your data could appear is a server log line described in section 6, which is not a record about you but a record about a request. The way to exercise a right is to ask - see section 11 - and the answer will be what actually happened rather than a form letter. If you are not satisfied with the answer, you have the right to complain to the supervisory authority in the EU member state where you live, work, or where the alleged infringement happened.</p><h2>11. Contact</h2><p>{{ contactRoute }}</p><p>Write to <a href="mailto:{{ contactEmail }}">{{ contactEmail }}</a>. Requests about a specific visit should include the approximate time and path requested; requests about a figure should include the page address, which names its own patch, region, queue and bracket.</p><h2>12. Changes to this policy</h2><p>This policy is explicitly amendable. It is reviewed whenever Riot updates its policies and on a fixed cadence, and the effective date at the top of the page changes when the text does. A change that affects what is collected will be written here before the change ships, not after.</p><h2>13. Trademarks and notices</h2><p>{{ trademark }}</p><p>{{ nonEndorsed }}</p><p>{{ riotNote .SiteURL }}</p><p>See also the <a href="/legal/terms">Terms of Service</a>, the <a href="/disclaimer">Disclaimer</a> and <a href="/about">how the numbers are produced</a>.</p></article>{{- end -}}
